// there are several different types in dyn

/* primative
	i8, i16, i32, i64, i128 = signed ints with 8-128bits
	u8, u16, u32, u64, u128 = unsigned ints with 8-128bits
	f32, f64 = floating point precision with single or double precision accoring to IEEE standards
	char = 8 bit ascii character
	bool = true or false bit
*/

*/ compound
	 () tuple type
	T[] array of type T
*/

*/ advanced
	*T pointer to type T
*/